Here are some thoughts on centralized grade tables. First of all they should be read-only. That is, a teacher can not directly modify them. The teacher would need to edit the grade within a given activity. This then raises the question of maintaining consistency between the centralized grade tables and the grades maintained by each activity, doing it in an efficient manner, and also maintaining compatiblility with the grade data stored within existing module instances. I propose three mechanisms for maintaining this consistency. First of all any student, when viewing an activity can click on a button which will synchronize the grade data for that activity with the central grade table in that course. Secondly any teacher, when viewing the gradebook, can click on a button to synchronize the grade data for all activities in the course with the central grade table. Thirdly the administrator can configure a cron job to synchronize grade data for a course or a category of courses. The gradebook should keep track of the last synchronization time for each activity and each activity should keep track of the latest grade entered/changed within that activity. Each activity module should have a library function 
